From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:29:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 077/138] drm: adp: t7000: Switch the layer through the param
 FIFO

On hw the layer-off write made from the VBI interrupt killed the pipe at
once (RdErr, frame counter frozen) with no flip in flight: on n61 the
ADP VBI fires at line 541 of 1334 (ADBE0 0x24 = 0x1021d), mid-scan, so
the write was not in the blanking at all.

iOS never writes LAYER_CTL directly while the pipe runs. Its blank frame
(and every swap) goes through the ADP param FIFO, which applies a packet
at a frame boundary and raises IRQ_STATUS bit 10. Do the same, with the
packet format of ADPParamFIFODriver::programFIFO: header
0x80000000 | sync << 30 | words << 16 | tag, then (count << 16) | offset
and the value for a run of ADP registers. Send it only when the FIFO is
idle (level 0x1040 == 0, ParmSt != 2; 1-2 ms sleeps, 100 ms max), enable
the packet-done bit for the wait (100 ms) and record the ADBE0 frame/line
register at send and completion time.

A layer-off packet that is not reported leaves the scanout on. A
layer-on packet that is not reported leaves the driver in the off state
(screen black, the next CRTC on or debugfs "power on" retries) instead
of falling back to a direct write. Without the IRQ the register is read
back once more, and a late-landing off packet is caught on the next on.

debugfs "power" also takes "nop" (header-only packet) and "same"
(LAYER_CTL = its current value), to check the packet path on hw before
anything visible changes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
